& [Purpose]
  + close the gap between an exact lexical SemanticAddress and the exact signed SOP bytes that address identifies
  + let a human or agent inspect current path line span text document digest certificate identity and projection proof without reopening files from the mutable workspace
  + preserve the Slice4B2A lexical result unchanged and make source projection an optional next stage

& [ProjectionForm]
  + VerifiedAnchorSourceProjection binds one exact SemanticAddress SourceAnchor signed source path exact UTF-8 quote document digest certificate id and projection digest
  + LexicalAnchorSourceProjectionResult binds the exact lexical lookup proof digest ordered projections fixed non-authority statement and a result proof digest
  + source path is package-relative human-readable metadata from the admitted SourceSnapshot and is not treated as an authorization or a live filesystem path
  + quote bytes come only from the admitted package QuoteRecord and are never reread from the current filesystem

& [ProjectionAlgorithm]
  + whole-validate the lexical result against request index catalogue and SemanticFabric before projection
  + for each ordered lexical match require the admitted package selected by unit id to equal the address package identity and digest
  + require the package QuoteRecord SourceAnchor to equal one exact address source anchor and require the source snapshot file identity to match
  + recompute document and span digests or reuse the existing admission proof only when whole package admission has already validated those exact bytes
  + decode quote bytes as UTF-8 and retain empty or multiline text exactly
  + produce one projection per match in match order and refuse any missing or conflicting source proof rather than omitting it
  + enforce positive bounded maximum projections maximum quote bytes and maximum serialized result bytes before returning success
  + compute domain-separated per-projection and complete-result digests and whole-replay exact equality

& [CLI]
  + extend only cantor-anchor-lab with optional --include-source
  + without the flag preserve exact Slice4B2A output bytes and behavior
  + with the flag return one closed JSON success envelope containing the original lookup result plus the verified source projection result
  + keep failures closed on stderr with exit code two and perform no write network provider service model or external process action

& [HonestyAndSecurity]
  + quoted text is proven to be the admitted package snapshot not asserted to equal the current mutable file or external reality
  + lexical selection still does not prove semantic purpose truth permission authority safety applicability lifecycle or boundary satisfaction
  + no path can escape into an unadmitted filesystem read because source bytes are selected only from the in-memory admitted package
  + any stale lookup proof package mismatch anchor mismatch missing quote invalid UTF-8 digest mismatch bound excess or replay difference refuses

& [Acceptance]
  + exact path lines bytes span document certificate package unit and lexical proof identities are visible
  + repeated equal inputs serialize byte-identically
  + projection order equals lexical match order and no match disappears under byte limits
  + mutated path text anchor digest certificate package order root or proof refuses under whole replay
  + tracked signed corpus CLI integration returns a nonempty verified source quotation for PreparedRuntime
  + focused debug release workspace Clippy format evidence diff exact-scanner and no-flag byte-stability gates pass

